  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the child as a representation of passive resignation",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual entity 'child' because the meme uses the child's pensive, resigned expression and passive posture as an analogical representation of the user's own potential state of mind — choosing to wait rather than engage further. The text 'i'll just wait here' is a first-person declaration that implicitly identifies the user as the one who will wait, making the child a visual stand-in for the user's own behavior or emotional state. This projection is not explicit with deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you' in the text, but the first-person perspective of the text creates a direct identification with the viewer/user.",
